Sval: expose WebMCP's modelContext only in agent tabs

Gecko gates navigator.modelContext on one global pref, so turning it on would
expose the API to every page in every workspace: a rare trait that marks Sval
users to trackers, and an API that changes how sites behave in the user's own
browsing. No chrome API can scope a WebIDL gate to a tab, so this adds a
parent-only BrowsingContext field, SvalAgentTab, that Sval sets on agent tabs,
and replaces the API's Pref= gates with a Func= check of the pref and the
top-level context's flag.

